  "prediction": "**United Airlines Introduces New Boarding Process and Expands Latin American Routes**\n\nUnited Airlines has made significant changes to its boarding process and expanded its routes in Latin America. The airline has introduced a new two-lane boarding system, which aims to reduce congestion and make the boarding process more efficient. The new system uses color-coded lanes and a staggered boarding call, with priority passengers boarding first.\n\nThe new boarding process was tested in a handful of gates in Chicago and Houston and has now been rolled out to all United locations. The airline has also introduced push notifications for passengers who have the mobile app, allowing them to receive updates on boarding times and flight delays.\n\nIn addition to the new boarding process, United has also expanded its routes in Latin America through a joint business agreement with Avianca and Copa Airlines. The agreement will provide customers with more choices and benefits, including integrated service, seamless travel, and reduced travel times.\n\nUnited carried close to 155 million passengers in the 12 months ended in August, a 6.1% increase from the previous year. The airline has been working to improve the boarding process and reduce congestion at gates, which has been a major complaint from customers.\n\nThe new boarding process has been well-received by customers, who have complained about clusters of travelers around gates. United's managing director of global operations strategy, Maria Walter, said that the new process will help to reduce congestion and make the boarding process more efficient.\n\nThe airline has also introduced a new system for its elite-level frequent flyers, who will now be able to pre-board before the official boarding call. The new system has been in effect at Los Angeles International Airport since February and will now be rolled out to all United locations.\n\nOverall, United's new boarding process and expanded Latin American routes are expected to provide customers with a more efficient and seamless travel experience.\n\n**Key Changes to United's Boarding Process:**\n\n* Two-lane boarding system with color-coded lanes\n* Staggered boarding call to reduce congestion\n* Priority passengers board first, including elite-level frequent flyers\n* Push notifications for passengers with the mobile app\n* Reduced boarding lanes to two from five\n\n**Expanded Latin American Routes:**\n\n* Joint business agreement with Avianca and Copa Airlines\n* Integrated service and seamless travel\n* Reduced travel times and more choices for customers\n* Expected to drive economic benefits and create new opportunities for the airline.",
